---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const CALENDLY = 'https://calendly.com/russell-decisive/30min';

const title = 'Finance for technology companies | Decisive';
const description =
  'Growth hides which customers and products actually pay. We find the profit behind the revenue, in dollars, in 14 days, on guarantee.';

const traps = [
  {
    name: 'Mental Accounting',
    body: 'A headline growth number hides which customers and products actually make money. The segment math never gets run, so the cross-subsidy compounds quietly, quarter after quarter.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Certainty Illusion',
    body: 'A dashboard full of green metrics can feel like proof the business is healthy. Some of those numbers stopped meaning money a while ago, and nobody is paid to notice.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Loss Aversion',
    body: 'The marquee customer you are most afraid to reprice or lose is often the one capping your margin. The math never gets run because the answer feels dangerous.',
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <header class="hero">
    <div class="hero-inner">
      <span class="eyebrow">For owner-led technology companies</span>
      <h1>
        <span class="h1-line">The growth chart is up.</span>
        <span class="h1-line h1-line-accent">The profit behind it is a guess.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="hero-subhead">
        Growth hides which customers and products actually pay. <span class="dollar">We find the profit behind the revenue, in dollars.</span> Guaranteed 3x your Diagnostic fee in recoverable value, in 14 days.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href={CALENDLY}>Book a fit call</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/how-it-works">See the 14-day Diagnostic</a>
      </div>
      <p class="hero-microcopy">30 minutes with Russ. No pitch. You leave knowing where to look first.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="container-narrow">
        <span class="section-eyebrow">Where the profit hides in a tech company</span>
        <h2>Revenue growth is easy to show. Profit truth is not.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Gross-margin quality, customer and segment profitability, retention economics, and what each channel really costs: the numbers that decide whether growth is making you money. Most dashboards track motion, not any of these.
        </p>
        <div class="category-pull">
          Your books tell you what happened. They can't tell you what to do next.
        </div>
        <p>
          The decisions weren't wrong. You made them on the only numbers you had, and those numbers were never built to decide from. Everyone who touches your books is paid to serve something else: the filing, the close, the report. Nobody is paid to make the next call defensible, and that is the job we do.
        </p>
        <div class="delay-callout">
          We don't audit the past. We make the next call defensible.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="traps">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-eyebrow">Where the value is trapped</div>
      <h2>Three traps behind a growth chart.</h2>
      <p class="lede" style="color: rgba(255,255,255,0.88);">
        The Six Trap Diagnostic&trade; reads your numbers through the decisions that produced them. Three of the six do the most damage in a technology company. The patterns are structural, not failures of the owner.
      </p>
      <div class="trap-grid">
        {traps.map((t, i) => (
          <div class="trap-card">
            <div class="trap-num">Trap {String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</div>
            <div class="trap-name">{t.name}</div>
            <p>{t.body}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <div class="traps-footer">
        We name the stack, price each one in dollars, and turn the read into a plan. We don't audit the past. We make the next call defensible.
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="container-narrow">
        <span class="section-eyebrow">Proof</span>
        <h2>The mechanism reads the same across industries, because the traps do.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="worked">
        <span class="label">Professional services, $30M revenue</span>
        <h4>A clean close is not a fast one, and neither tells you where the cash is stuck.</h4>
        <p>
          Cash was trapped in a billing and close cadence nobody had revisited, and clean-looking reports masked the leak. We rebuilt the rhythm, pulled the working capital forward, and put margin on a weekly line of sight. Recurring-revenue businesses run the same play.
        </p>
        <div class="calc">
          <div><span class="k">Working capital recovered</span><span class="v accent">$380,000</span></div>
          <div><span class="k">Close time</span><span class="v">22 to 3 days</span></div>
          <div><span class="k">Margin improvement</span><span class="v">~$50,000 / mo</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="font-size: 14px; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 22px;">
        Anonymized by segment and revenue band until attribution is confirmed.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="container-narrow">
        <span class="section-eyebrow">Tiers and pricing</span>
        <h2>Find. Install. Run.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Most owners start with the 14-day Decision Diagnostic and move into the 90-Day Resolution. Pricing is banded by revenue, and the floor is $5M.
        </p>
        <p class="promise-line">
          The Diagnostic promise: at least 3x the fee in owner-accepted value identified by Day 14, or you pay nothing.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-cta-row" style="margin-top: 8px;">
          <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/#tiers">See tiers and pricing</a>
          <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/guarantee">Read the guarantee</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="close-section">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="section-eyebrow">Book a fit call</span>
      <h2>Decide from the numbers. Prove it in the cash.</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        In 14 days you know what your money is actually doing, in dollars: the traps that are running, the recoverable value, and the first three moves, whether or not we ever work together again. It starts with one 30-minute call.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href={CALENDLY}>Book a fit call</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/how-it-works">See the 14-day Diagnostic</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero-microcopy { font-size: 15px; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.7); margin: 10px 0 0; }
  .promise-line { font-family: Inter, sans-serif; font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); margin-top: 8px; }
</style>
